ned-off-by: Philipp Zabel &lt;p.zabel@pengutronix.de&gt; (cherry picked from commit 515ba6a59cbab44c989f25b2518b82491deb832e  git://git.pengutronix.de/git/pza/linux.git tags/mediatek-drm-fixes-2016-06-01) Signed-off-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:40529 TEST=build and boot oak &amp; elm  Change-Id: I677c1cb78ced33f844c1bd5fa2aabeb22918ebb8 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/349000 Commit-Ready: PC Liao &lt;pc.liao@mediatek.com&gt; Commit-Ready: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: PC Liao &lt;pc.liao@mediatek.com&gt; Tested-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Bibby Hsieh &lt;bibby.hsieh@mediatek.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="349000" owner_email="bibby.hsieh@mediatek.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="7" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/00/349000/7" remote="cros" total_fail_count="5"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I211c3798e03cb6b0f39dd0f4321591867e526b9b" commit="1e85e7844701513cf5daddf01bfaa3a34ac77f66" commit_message="UPSTREAM: drm/mediatek: mtk_dsi: Remove spurious drm_connector_unregister  Connectors are unregistered by mtk_drm_drv via drm_connector_unregister_all().  Signed-off-by: Philipp Zabel &lt;p.zabel@pengutronix.de&gt; (cherry picked from commit 2ea9f31799adce35d8c9a0bb3bc1d2b515702c6f  git://git.pengutronix.de/git/pza/linux.git tags/mediatek-drm-fixes-2016-06-01) Signed-off-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:40529 TEST=build and boot oak &amp; elm  Change-Id: I211c3798e03cb6b0f39dd0f4321591867e526b9b Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/348981 Commit-Ready: PC Liao &lt;pc.liao@mediatek.com&gt; Commit-Ready: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: PC Liao &lt;pc.liao@mediatek.com&gt; Tested-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Bibby Hsieh &lt;bibby.hsieh@mediatek.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="348981" owner_email="djkurtz@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="6" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/81/348981/6" remote="cros" total_fail_count="5"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I63b6b3bdcbd6e411f2676203819e709c6def8d3a" commit="2c16876d0c9a992b0695ab16e86b8fcfec54af5f" commit_message="BACKPORT: FROMLIST: drm/mediatek: Add HDMI support  This patch adds drivers for the HDMI bridge connected to the DPI0 display subsystem function block, for the HDMI DDC block, and for the HDMI PHY to support HDMI output.  Signed-off-by: Jie Qiu &lt;jie.qiu@mediatek.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Philipp Zabel &lt;p.zabel@pengutronix.de&gt; (am from https://patchwork.kernel.org/patch/9137093/) Signed-off-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; [djkurtz: Sync chromeos-3.18 to FROMLIST v15]  BUG=chrome-os-partner:40529 TEST=build and boot oak-tot to UI  Change-Id: I63b6b3bdcbd6e411f2676203819e709c6def8d3a Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/347712 Commit-Ready: PC Liao &lt;pc.liao@mediatek.com&gt; Commit-Ready: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: PC Liao &lt;pc.liao@mediatek.com&gt; Tested-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Bibby Hsieh &lt;bibby.hsieh@mediatek.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="347712" owner_email="bibby.hsieh@mediatek.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/12/347712/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="4"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I307fca80f93c13e10c7fc6e780f72dca4c7a1b28" commit="8f5d986c7aa185bb95686a1292e8bc00bcab7380" commit_message="FIXUP: FROMLIST: drm/bridge: Add I2C based driver for ps8640 bridge  chromeos-3.18 currently has FROMLIST v15 of the PS8640 driver. This version is incompatible with UPSTREAM version of the Mediatek DRM driver.  To quote Philipp Zabel: &quot;The main DRM driver mtk_drm_drv now calls drm_connector_register_all() after drm_dev_register() in the mtk_drm_bind() function. That function should iterate over all connectors and call drm_connector_register() for each of them. The call to drm_connector_init() from mtk_hdmi_bridge_attach() should be enough to make this happen.  The drm_connector_(un)register calls also have to be removed from the ps8640 driver.&quot;  Signed-off-by: Jitao Shi &lt;jitao.shi@mediatek.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:40529 TEST=build and boot oak &amp; elm TEST=suspend &amp; resume =&gt; check internal display TEST=backlight_dbus_tool --set  --percent=0  =&gt; confirm internal display turns off TEST=backlight_dbus_tool --set  --percent=100  =&gt; confirm internal display turns back on  Change-Id: I307fca80f93c13e10c7fc6e780f72dca4c7a1b28 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/348996 Commit-Ready: PC Liao &lt;pc.liao@mediatek.com&gt; Commit-Ready: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: PC Liao &lt;pc.liao@mediatek.com&gt; Tested-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="348996" owner_email="jitao.shi@mediatek.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="7" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/96/348996/7" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Ic792f811130f5ebfe04188a9abd02c9a480cfcb2" commit="ab3a37b81647f3b7be5a28c928326b3d7d4f1a1b" commit_message="FIXUP: FROMLIST: drm: bridge: anx78xx: Add anx78xx driver support.  chromeos-3.18 currently has FROMLIST v3 of the ANX78xx driver. This version is incompatible with UPSTREAM version of the Mediatek DRM driver.  To quote Philipp Zabel: &quot;The main DRM driver mtk_drm_drv now calls drm_connector_register_all() after drm_dev_register() in the mtk_drm_bind() function. That function should iterate over all connectors and call drm_connector_register() for each of them. The call do drm_connector_init() from mtk_hdmi_bridge_attach() should be enough to make this happen.  The drm_connector_(un)register calls also have to be removed from the anx78xx driver.&quot;  Fixes: 4b29b8d FROMLIST: drm: bridge: anx78xx: Add anx78xx bridge driver support. Signed-off-by: Jitao Shi &lt;jitao.shi@mediatek.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:40529 TEST=build and boot oak &amp; elm  w/ HDMI plugged in native port  w/ Type-C display  w/out external display TEST=suspend &amp; resume w/ external display TEST=suspend &amp; resume w/out external display  Change-Id: Ic792f811130f5ebfe04188a9abd02c9a480cfcb2 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/348997 Commit-Ready: PC Liao &lt;pc.liao@mediatek.com&gt; Commit-Ready: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: PC Liao &lt;pc.liao@mediatek.com&gt; Tested-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="348997" owner_email="jitao.shi@mediatek.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="9" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/97/348997/9" remote="cros" total_fail_count="3"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2016.05" change_id="Id3c6c270774108e4caf56e2a07c5072edc65bb58" commit="14a5ce404fa95117bd4460c96206f51f7d642d11" commit_message="UPSTREAM: intel/apollolake: Clear TSEG reg early in bootblock  TSEG register comes out of reset with a non-zero default value. This causes issues when cbmem_top returns non-zero value based on TSEG read before DRAM is initialized. Thus, clear TSEG reg early in bootblock to avoid unwanted side-effects.  Change-Id: Id3c6c270774108e4caf56e2a07c5072edc65bb58 Signed-off-by: Furquan Shaikh &lt;furquan@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://review.coreboot.org/15049 Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: build bot (Jenkins) Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/349431 Commit-Ready: Furquan Shaikh &lt;furquan@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Furquan Shaikh &lt;furquan@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="349431" owner_email="furquan@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/31/349431/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2016.05" change_id="I0424a00753d06e26639750f065a7a08a710bfaba" commit="a2424dd8c4cf26ba2d6b9aff74a8f1c11231eebb" commit_message="UPSTREAM: intel/fsp_baytrail/i2c: mask i2c interrupts in i2c_init()  i2c_init() leaves the I2C device enabled. Combined with the default interrupt mask (0x8ff) and the fact that the interrupt line is shared, this leads to an interrupt storm in the OS until a proper I2C driver is loaded.  This change clears the interrupt mask to prevent the interrupt storm.  Change-Id: I0424a00753d06e26639750f065a7a08a710bfaba Signed-off-by: Ben Gardner &lt;gardner.ben@gmail.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://review.coreboot.org/15047 Tested-by: build bot (Jenkins) Reviewed-by: Duncan Laurie &lt;dlaurie@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Werner Zeh &lt;werner.zeh@siemens.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/349432 Commit-Ready: Furquan Shaikh &lt;furquan@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Furquan Shaikh &lt;furquan@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="349432" owner_email="furquan@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/32/349432/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2016.05" change_id="I149fcfe2ad72fe3d7390ee2043a86432aeae3f08" commit="c7cc7e2542c6104625c046f5be0cab187d23f576" commit_message="UPSTREAM: AGESA boards: Drop unused include  These files do not use definitions from OptionsIds.h. Also those definitions are required and already included for Ids.h.  Change-Id: I149fcfe2ad72fe3d7390ee2043a86432aeae3f08 Signed-off-by: Kysti Mlkki &lt;kyosti.malkki@gmail.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://review.coreboot.org/14980 Tested-by: build bot (Jenkins) Reviewed-by: Martin Roth &lt;martinroth@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/349433 Commit-Ready: Furquan Shaikh &lt;furquan@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Furquan Shaikh &lt;furquan@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="349433" owner_email="furquan@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/33/349433/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I7dd703e38c68306eb10b19ffbacb59885134acf2" commit="e1dbfa711da9c9e1eecf808c782d62947ed4908a" commit_message="CHROMIUM: thermal: mtk driver depends on CPU_FREQ and must be built into kernel  The folowing build errors are seen on test builds trying to build the mediatek thermal driver as module and with CPU_FREQ not enabled.  drivers/thermal/mtk_thermal.c: In function 'mtk_svs_hw_init': drivers/thermal/mtk_thermal.c:1107:3: error:  implicit declaration of function 'cpufreq_get_policy' drivers/thermal/mtk_thermal.c:1136:3: error:  implicit declaration of function 'cpufreq_update_policy' drivers/thermal/mtk_thermal.c: At top level: drivers/thermal/mtk_thermal.c:1485:1: error:    redefinition of '__inittest' drivers/thermal/mtk_thermal.c:1281:1: note:  previous definition of '__inittest' was here drivers/thermal/mtk_thermal.c:1485:1: error:  redefinition of 'init_module' drivers/thermal/mtk_thermal.c:1281:1: note:  previous definition of 'init_module' was here  Commit 5be71f4c13d3 (&quot;BACKPORT: FROMLIST: PM / AVS: thermal: MT8173: Introduce support for SVS engine&quot;) introduces calls into the CPU frequency code, thus adding a dependency of the Mediatek thermal driver on CPU_FREQ. It also adds a late_initcall(), which in modular builds is mapped to module_init(). This conflicts with the already existing module initialization.  BUG=chromium:616355 TEST=Try to build as module; try to build with CPU_FREQ disabled  Fixes: 5be71f4c13d3 (&quot;BACKPORT: FROMLIST: PM / AVS: thermal: MT8173: Introduce support for SVS engine&quot;) Change-Id: I7dd703e38c68306eb10b19ffbacb59885134acf2 Signed-off-by: Guenter Roeck &lt;groeck@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/348651 Reviewed-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="348651" owner_email="groeck@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/51/348651/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><lkgm version="8406.0.0-rc2"/></manifest>